Copyright (c) 2026 guhhammer. All rights reserved, except as granted below.

This licence covers lore: its code, documentation and own writing in this
repository, from version 0.4.7 on. Versions up to 0.4.6 were released under
the MIT licence and stay under it. Material made by others keeps its own
licence (section 6).

1. Use. Anyone may install and run lore, free of charge, for any purpose,
   at home or at work.

2. Sharing copies. You may share exact, unchanged copies of lore (its source
   as published in https://github.com/guhhammer/lore, or the files of its
   releases), as long as you charge nothing for them and keep this licence
   with them. Package managers and registries may carry such copies on the
   same terms.

3. Changes. You may change lore only to contribute the change to this
   project through its GitHub repository, for example in a pull request.
   You may not publish, share or distribute a changed version of lore, or a
   work based on it, without the copyright holder's written consent.

4. Selling. You may not sell lore, a changed version of it, or access to
   it, nor include it in something you sell, without the copyright holder's
   written consent.

5. Contributions. By sending a contribution to this project (a pull
   request, a patch, a page, a translation), you confirm that you have the
   right to send it, and you give the copyright holder a perpetual,
   worldwide, free, irrevocable licence to use, change, relicense and
   distribute it, as part of lore or otherwise. You keep the copyright to
   your contribution.

6. Other people's material. These keep their own licences, which this one
   does not restrict:
   - the usage examples and translations adapted from tldr-pages
     (content/), under CC BY 4.0;
   - the pages from Learn X in Y minutes (languages/), under CC BY-SA 3.0;
   - the libraries lore is built with, under their own licences.
   Their notices are in the README and in the folders that hold them.

7. Consent. To ask for consent to change, share or sell lore beyond this
   licence, open an issue in the GitHub repository above.

8. Ending. If you break this licence, the rights it gives you end. They come
   back if you stop within 30 days of being told.

9. No warranty. lore is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind,
   express or implied, including the warranties of merchantability, fitness
   for a particular purpose and noninfringement. In no event shall the
   copyright holder or the contributors be liable for any claim, damages or
   other liability, whether in an action of contract, tort or otherwise,
   arising from, out of or in connection with lore or its use.
